cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "FunctionalDiagrams: functional derivatives and Feynman diagrams in Mathematica"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Africani
    given-names: Nazzareno
    affiliation: "SISSA, Trieste"
version: 2.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/n4sd4q/FunctionalDiagrams"
url: "https://github.com/n4sd4q/FunctionalDiagrams"
abstract: >-
  A Mathematica package that takes functional derivatives of generating functionals and effective actions
  symbolically, with the signs of fermions, and writes the results as Feynman diagrams with their weights: perturbation
  theory, classes of diagrams, the 1PI and 2PI effective actions, the Luttinger-Ward functional, Bethe-Salpeter and
  parquet equations, Hedin's equations, pictures in TikZ, and the evaluation of diagrams in Matsubara frequency and in
  dimensional regularization.
keywords:
  - functional derivatives
  - Feynman diagrams
  - many-body perturbation theory
  - Luttinger-Ward functional
  - parquet equations
  - Hedin's equations
  - GW approximation
  - Matsubara sums
  - 2PI effective action
  - Nambu-Gor'kov superfield
  - dimensional regularization
  - quantum electrodynamics
  - Mathematica
